    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.hunter.io/v2/email-verifier",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [{ "name": "email", "value": "={{ $json.body.email }}" }]
        },
        "options": { "response": { "response": { "neverError": true } } }
      },
      "id": "apollo-enrich-001",
      "name": "Hunter Verify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [176, 112],
      "notes": "neverError so an enrichment failure degrades the score rather than killing the lead."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=BUYER FORM SUBMISSION:\n{{ JSON.stringify($('Buyer Lead In').item.json.body) }}\n\nHUNTER EMAIL VERIFICATION (may be partial):\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.data || $json) }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a senior real estate sales qualifier. A potential property BUYER filled a landing-page form, and we ALSO verified their email via Hunter.io.\n\nHunter returns signals such as: status (valid / invalid / accept_all / webmail / disposable / unknown), a deliverability score 0-100, whether the address is webmail (gmail/yahoo = personal), disposable (throwaway), and sometimes a company/organisation tied to the domain.\n\nUse BOTH signals to qualify the lead:\n1. STATED INTENT (form): budget, location, property type, bedrooms, timeline, financing readiness, message.\n2. EMAIL EVIDENCE (Hunter): A VALID, deliverable email = a real, reachable lead (good). A DISPOSABLE or INVALID email = likely fake or low-intent (lower the score significantly). A COMPANY-DOMAIN email suggests a working professional (some ability-to-pay signal) versus generic free webmail (neutral, common, fine). A low deliverability score means you may never reach them, so lower the score.\n\nNormalise: budget_band, preferred_location, property_type, bedrooms, timeline, financing_ready. Capture from Hunter: email_status, email_deliverable (yes/no), email_type (corporate/webmail/disposable/unknown), company (from domain if present, else blank).\n\nScore 0-100 on readiness-to-transact, weighing intent (urgency, clear budget, financing, specific need) AND email evidence (real, deliverable, professional = higher; disposable/invalid = much lower). Label hot (80+) / warm (50-79) / cold (<50). Note missing info, recommend the single best next action, and draft a short, warm, personalised first follow-up message ready to send. Be realistic — clear intent + valid email = hot; vague intent + disposable email = cold. Do not inflate.",
          "passthroughBinaryImages": true
        }
      },
      "id": "98f1349d-fd84-4741-a9f5-900fd046babe",
      "name": "AI Lead Qualifier",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
